v1.3.4 (2026-05-11)
-------------------
Installer completely rewritten for reliability on any Windows PC:

Installer (setup.nsi):
- Python: winget is now the primary install method (built into Windows 10/11,
  silent, system-wide, no TLS issues); falls back to python.org download only
  if winget is unavailable
- Python packages: installed from bundled offline wheels (6.2 MB included in
  installer) — no internet required for pip, no SSL/proxy failures possible
- OpenVPN Connect: installed via winget if not already present (non-fatal;
  installer completes even if winget fails)
- Removed Yubico PIV Tool install — yubikit speaks Windows Smart Card directly,
  no extra tool needed; libykcs11.dll still copied opportunistically if already
  present
- Removed NSISdl downloads (TLS 1.2 incompatible); all downloads use PowerShell
  Invoke-WebRequest
- FindPython no longer uses 'where python' (avoids Windows Store stub at
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\WindowsApps\python.exe which is not a real Python)

Registration page:
- Installer download link now uses /api/register/{token}/installer so the
  downloaded file is named VPNSetup-TOKEN.exe (token is embedded in filename)
- When OpenVPN Connect auto-import fails, shows winget install command and
  explains how to open the downloaded .ovpn manually
- No other UI changes

v1.3.3 (2026-05-11)
-------------------
Completed end-to-end automated YubiKey registration flow:

Registration flow:
- register.html: certificate is now generated automatically on page load
  (no separate "Generate Certificate" button); user sees a single action:
  "Program my YubiKey"
- register.html: success panel now branches on ovpn_imported — if the helper
  auto-imported the .ovpn into OpenVPN Connect, shows "profile imported,
  open OpenVPN Connect and enter your PIN"; otherwise shows manual download
  button
- register.html: onHelperLaunch() polls every 2s for up to 30s after user
  clicks "Start VPN Helper" so the page reacts immediately when helper starts
- vpnweb-helper.py: after programming the YubiKey, downloads the .ovpn and
  opens it via os.startfile() (Windows file association → OpenVPN Connect);
  returns ovpn_imported: true/false in the /setup response

Installer:
- setup.nsi: pre-starts vpnweb-helper.py at end of install (via pythonw)
  so helper is already running when user clicks the registration link
- setup.nsi: updated finish message — "Insert your YubiKey, then open the
  registration link from your email"
- VPNSetup.exe: 174 KB compiled installer, served at /static/VPNSetup.exe

Email:
- Invite email redesigned: Step 1 = installer download link, Step 2 =
  registration link; clear instructions matching the automated flow
- HTML email: styled two-step layout with download button and registration
  link button
